    <string name="tut_welcome_title">Welcome</string>
    <string name="tut_welcome_body">A quick tour of the workflow: first you set up your Workshop, then you calculate in Calculate. You can close it any time.</string>
    <string name="tut_stock_title">Workshop › Raw stock</string>
    <string name="tut_stock_body">Save your suppliers and the raw material you buy (bars, plates, profiles) with its price. That is what drives each piece\'s cost.</string>
    <string name="tut_machines_title">Workshop › Machines</string>
    <string name="tut_machines_body">Register your lathes and milling machines, conventional or CNC, with their RPM, feeds and capacity. When calculating, the machine is the first thing you pick.</string>
    <string name="tut_machining_title">Workshop › Machining</string>
    <string name="tut_machining_body">Add the materials you machine and your inserts or end mills with manufacturer values. If you don\'t have them, the app uses conservative generic HSS and carbide profiles.</string>
    <string name="tut_calc_stock_title">Calculate › Raw stock</string>
    <string name="tut_calc_stock_body">Pick the part\'s shape, enter its dimensions and the material: you get volume, weight and cost.</string>
    <string name="tut_calc_machining_title">Calculate › Turning and milling</string>
    <string name="tut_calc_machining_body">Tap the title at the top to switch mode. Follow the steps in order: machine, operation (with icons), material and tool, and finally the dimensions. You get RPM, feed and cutting time.</string>
    <string name="tut_settings_title">Settings</string>
    <string name="tut_settings_body">Change language, units and currency here, and back up your data. You can repeat this tutorial from this screen.</string>
